# Prefer Private Build Methods for Tiny UI Pieces

**Rule:** When a small UI component serves only the current widget and is not reused anywhere else, prefer a private `_buildX(...)` method returning a `Widget` inside the parent class rather than extracting a separate `StatelessWidget`. Extracting a class for something used once adds redundant internal classes and fragments closely-related build logic.

Note: this concerns tiny presentational pieces. Non-widget helper classes (`CustomClipper`, `CustomPainter`, `Delegate`) still follow the one-class-per-file rule.

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
class GuideList extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => ListView.builder(
        itemBuilder: (_, i) => _StepItem(index: i),
      );
}

class _StepItem extends StatelessWidget { // used once, still a class
  final int index;
  const _StepItem({required this.index});
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Text('Step $index');
}
```

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
class GuideList extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => ListView.builder(
        itemBuilder: (context, i) => _buildStepItem(context, i),
      );

  Widget _buildStepItem(BuildContext context, int index) => Text('Step $index');
}
```
